      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for your advice:\nRegarding skipping dm-verity verification:\nIn our custom module, we ensure that dm-verity verification is always performed. Also skipping this check will not be intercepted by CTS/VTS tests.\n\nRegarding try_verify_in_tasklet:\nThis appears to trigger the queue_work(system_bh_wq, \u0026io-\u003ebh_work) logic in verity_end_io. We don’t fully understand the significance of system_bh_wq here: What makes this workqueue special, and how does it improve performance?",
